{
  "description": "EventBus (plan §11.2, §25): lives on the engine executor. publish(type, data) gives the event the next seq (firstSeq, firstSeq + 1, …; lastSeq is firstSeq - 1 before the first) and the clock's now as 'at', keeps the last 'retain' events for replays, hands it to every in-engine subscriber whose types include it (all types when none are given, internal ones too) and queues it on every stream that wants it. Delivery is in seq order for every subscriber: an event published by a handler is delivered once the current event has reached every subscriber. A subscriber added during a delivery gets only events published after it subscribed; one removed during a delivery gets nothing more, even the event being delivered. Streams (the server's SSE) carry client-visible events only (never leaseChanged or stepFinished, whatever their types ask for). stream(after, types): with after null only events published from now on; otherwise first the retained events with seq > after; when after is beyond lastSeq (an id from an earlier engine), or events after it are no longer retained, or there are more of them than the stream's capacity, the stream starts with one resync item instead (the reader then sends a snapshot). A stream holds at most 'streamCapacity' items: when an event doesn't fit, everything queued is replaced by one resync item. Whenever a resync item waits on a stream, the events published until the reader takes it are dropped: the snapshot the reader then sends covers them. close() ends a stream: what was queued is dropped and the reader sees its end. The harness runs the ops in order on a manual clock that starts at 2026-10-02T20:00:00.000Z. Ops: publish {type, data (default {})}; advance <ms> (the clock); subscribe {as, types, onReceive: {type, do: [ops]}} (onReceive runs its ops each time that subscriber receives an event of that type); unsubscribe <as>; stream {as, after, types}; read <as> (takes every item queued on the stream, without waiting: 'resync', '<seq> <type>', or 'end' once closed); close <as>. Expect: received {<as>: ['<seq> <type>', …]}, read {<as>: […]} (everything read from it, in order), lastSeq, events (EngineEvent.json of every published event, in order).",
  "functions": [
    "EventBus.publish",
    "EventBus.subscribe",
    "EventBus.stream",
    "EventBus.lastSeq",
    "Subscription.cancel",
    "EventStream.poll",
    "EventStream.close",
    "EngineEvent.json"
  ],
